 :root-cause
 "The public can? entry point classified whether the permission root existed, then generated-authoritative can* immediately repeated the same schema-generation lookup before selecting the generated indexed engine. The corrected steady-state harness measured three stable GitHub Actions batch medians between 1004.884 and 1006.3265 microseconds, proving that the earlier one-batch miss was not only a tiered-compilation transition."
 :fix
 "Hoist the already computed permission-root fact across the public/generated dispatch. A defined root enters generated traversal directly; an undefined root returns false without compiling an invalid plan. Dafny proves result preservation under the established undefined-root-denies contract and proves one root lookup for a generated-authoritative public check. A public-client regression observes exactly one lookup."
 :closing-evidence
